# LF in the working tree, always — on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf
# says locally. This is not a style preference: with autocrlf=true a Windows
# clone gets CRLF, and vitest's transform then fails to parse the script
# modules whose templates emit regex literals (tests/families.test.js and four
# others die with "Invalid or unexpected token"). A fresh clone must be able to
# run `npm test` and pass.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries — never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webm binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite binary
